Historical Luminary assembly is public domain, with original MIT Museum,
Paul Fjeld, Deborah Douglas, Ron Burkey and transcription contributor notices
retained in the historical files. The native routines translate that historical
source; no Virtual AGC instruction implementation is copied into the native core.

tools/reference_runner.c is GPL-2.0-or-later, because its host executable links
to Virtual AGC GPL-2.0-or-later objects. The GPL test executable is generated
locally and not distributed here. GPL-2.0 text is supplied in tools/COPYING.GPL-2.0.
The MIT test input code can be included in that GPL host executable. This does
not introduce a Virtual AGC link or GPL implementation into the native C64 PRG.

External LLVM-MOS, Virtual AGC, VICE, and Commodore ROMs retain their own licenses.
Their binaries and ROMs are not redistributed in this repository or handoff.
